The base of a number string should be base-ten, unless:
* explicitly specified by ju'u, AND/OR
* the string contains hexadecimal digits, in which case it is defaults to hexadecimal, AND/OR
* overridden by context

It should not be necessary to state this in the cmavo definitions here, but rather in the definition for ju'u.

I assume that it is unnecessary to formally define the mechanism of big-endian positional notation. At any rate, I am unable to do so myself.

!Usage for decimal digits
''cacra li revo .a li pare''%%%
It lasts for 24 or 12 hours.

''mi tatpi .i li paci vi tcika''%%%
I'm tired. It's 13 o'clock here.

''li paze pi'e ci''%%%
17:03

!Usage for hexadecimal digits
''li dau re ci vai vai vai vai vai''%%%
A23FFFFF


!Proposed definitions

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: no (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 0. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 0
* zero
* no
* none
* nought
* nil
!!!Usage Examples
;no jbopre cu tavla .uinai:''No Lojbanist is talking. *sadness*''
;lo nu mi jmive li re no cu nanca:''The event of me living is twenty years in duration. / I am 20 years old.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: pa (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 1. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 1
* one
* single
!!!Usage Examples
;xu su'o pa jbopre cu jundi:''Is it true that at least one Lojbanist is paying attention?''
;sipna ze'u lo cacra be li pa no:''Slept for the long duration of 10 hours.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: re (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 2. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 2
* two
!!!Usage Examples
;mi se mensi re da:''I have (exactly) two sisters.''
;lo nu mi jmive li re no cu nanca:''The event of me living is twenty years in duration. / I am 20 years old.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ci (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 3. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 3
* three
!!!Usage Examples
;mi re moi lo ci mei:''I am the second of the three.''
;re lo ci gerku cu blabi:''Two of the three dogs are white.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: vo (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 4. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 4
* four
!!!Usage Examples
;ca tcika fa li pa vo pi'e mu mu:''It's currently 14:55 o'clock.''
;mi morji gi'e djuno vau lo du'u li re su'i re li vo du:''I remember and know that 2 + 2 = 4.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: mu (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 5. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 5
* five
!!!Usage Examples
;ca tcika fa li pa vo pi'e mu mu:''It's currently 14:55 o'clock.''
;by mrobi'o de'i li pa ze mu no pi'e ze pi'e re bi:''B died on 1750-7-28.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: xa (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 6. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 6
* six
!!!Usage Examples
;li xa pi'e vo so tcika fo mi:''It is 6:49 o'clock at my place.''
;li ze pa mu pi'i re xa mu du li xo:''715 × 265 = what number?''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: ze (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 7. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 7 
* seven
!!!Usage Examples
;re'o lo bitmu ze cmalu ckana cu linji se punji gi'e se gacri lo snime blabi boxfo:''Adjacent to the wall, seven small beds were placed in line and covered with snow white sheets.''
;by mrobi'o de'i li pa ze mu no pi'e ze pi'e re bi:''B died on 1750-7-28.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: bi (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 8. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 8
* eight
!!!Usage Examples
;by mrobi'o de'i li pa ze mu no pi'e ze pi'e re bi:''B died on 1750-7-28.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: so (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Digit 9. 
!!!Proposed Keywords
* 9
* nine
!!!Usage Examples
;li xa pi'e vo so tcika fo mi:''It is 6:49 o'clock at my place.''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: dau (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Hexadecimal digit A (decimal 10).
!!!Proposed Keywords
* A ; hexadecimal
* ten ; hexadecimal
!!!Usage Examples
;li dau re ci vai vai vai vai vai:''A23FFFFF (hexadecimal)''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: fei (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Hexadecimal digit B (decimal 11).
!!!Proposed Keywords
* B ; hexadecimal
* eleven ; hexadecimal
!!!Usage Examples
;li dau fei gai jau rei vai:''ABCDEF (hexadecimal)''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: gai (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Hexadecimal digit C (decimal 12).
!!!Proposed Keywords
* C ; hexadecimal
* twelve ; hexadecimal
!!!Usage Examples
;li dau fei gai jau rei vai:''ABCDEF (hexadecimal)''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: jau (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Hexadecimal digit D (decimal 13).
!!!Proposed Keywords
* D ; hexadecimal
* thirteen ; hexadecimal
!!!Usage Examples
;li dau fei gai jau rei vai:''ABCDEF (hexadecimal)''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: rei (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Hexadecimal digit E (decimal 14).
!!!Proposed Keywords
* E ; hexadecimal
* fourteen ; hexadecimal
!!!Usage Examples
;li dau fei gai jau rei vai:''ABCDEF (hexadecimal)''
{BOX}

{BOX()}
!!cmavo: vai (PA1)
!!!Proposed Definition
Hexadecimal digit F (decimal 15).
!!!Proposed Keywords
* F ; hexadecimal
* fifteen ; hexadecimal
!!!Usage Examples
;li dau re ci vai vai vai vai vai:''A23FFFFF (hexadecimal)''
{BOX}

!Interactions with other sections
The sections with ju'u should state that digits are in base-ten, unless they contain at least one hexadecimal digit, or they are explicitly specified by ju'u, or the base is overriden by context.

!Impact
None intended.